title: Financial Aid Applications Are Open
---
author: ORGANIZERS
---
pub_date: 2026-10-21
---
body:

We want PyCon DE 2027 to be accessible to everyone, regardless of financial circumstances. Our [Financial Aid Programme](/financial-aid/) is open, and if money is what stands between you and Heidelberg, we'd love to hear from you.

**Deadline: 27 December 2026, 23:59 CET.**

## What we offer

- **Online ticket:** a free standard online ticket
- **In-person ticket:** a free standard in-person ticket
- **Europe and neighbouring countries travel grant:** up to 250 € in travel reimbursements, plus an on-site ticket and hotel accommodation
- **Intercontinental travel grant:** up to 650 € in travel reimbursements, plus an on-site ticket and hotel accommodation

We pre-book shared hotel rooms near the venue, which secures better rates and gives you documentation for a visa application. Prefer to arrange your own stay? Tell us in the form, and we can reimburse up to 150 € for accommodation.

## Who should apply

Anyone who needs financial assistance. When reviewing applications, we consider:

- **Economic factors:** students, job seekers and anyone facing financial hardship are encouraged to apply.
- **Diversity:** we actively support applicants who help make our community more inclusive and representative.
- **Community contributions:** tell us how you give back, through open-source projects, local meetups or other initiatives.

If you don't receive an in-person grant, you remain eligible for a free online ticket.

## Planning to give a talk?

Speakers don't receive travel support automatically. The [Call for Proposals](/call-for-proposals/) opens on 4 November. If you need financial assistance to present in Heidelberg, apply to the programme right after you submit your proposal. Don't wait for the acceptance notification.

## Timeline

- **27 December 2026, 23:59 CET:** Application deadline
- **20 January 2027:** Applicants are notified

Please respond to your offer within seven days, otherwise the grant goes to someone else.

## Good to know

- Travel costs are reimbursed after the conference, against approved receipts, by bank transfer or PayPal.
- We prioritise low-carbon travel: trains are preferred, and flights may be declined where a sustainable alternative is readily available.
- Need a visa for Germany? Request an invitation letter and book your embassy appointment as early as possible.
- The [Masterclasses](/masterclasses/) day on 19 April is not covered by the grant.

[Read the full details](/financial-aid/) and [apply now](https://forms.gle/KUZRET7b7u19bUtf9).

Want to help more people attend? You or your company can become a [Diversity Sponsor](/sponsoring/).

— The PyCon DE Team
